# Vydon Go Rules

## Formatting

- `gofmt` + `goimports` + `golines --max-len=140` are the source of truth.
- `interface{}` is auto-rewritten to `any` by gofmt — write `any` directly.
- Imports are grouped (stdlib / external / internal) separated by blank lines.

## Linters (`.golangci.yaml`)

`bodyclose`, `errcheck`, `forbidigo`, `goconst`, `gocritic`, `gosec`, `govet`, `ineffassign`, `misspell`, `nakedret`, `noctx`, `nolintlint`, `revive`, `staticcheck`, `unconvert`, `unparam`, `unused`, `usestdlibvars`, `whitespace`, `mnd`.

- `gocyclo` complexity limit: 10.
- `funlen` statement limit: 50.
- `goconst` triggers after 10 occurrences.
- `//nolint:<linter>` is acceptable when justified by a comment above; bare `//nolint` is rejected.

## Errors

- Wrap with `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`. Never `errors.New(err.Error())`.
- Check with `errors.Is` / `errors.As`. Never compare error strings.
- Reserve `panic` for `init()` and contract violations. `log.Fatal` is allowed only in `main`.
- Ignoring an error must be explicit: `_ = f()`.

## Logging

- `log/slog` only. No `log` stdlib, no `zap`, no `logrus`.
- Always pass context: `logger.InfoContext(ctx, "msg", "key", value)`.
- No `fmt.Println` in production code.

## Concurrency

- `ctx context.Context` is the first parameter and never stored in a struct.
- Pair every `context.WithCancel` / `WithTimeout` with `defer cancel()` on the next line.
- Use `errgroup.WithContext` instead of raw goroutines + `sync.WaitGroup`.
- Channels in API signatures have explicit direction (`<-chan T`, `chan<- T`).

## HTTP and SQL

- `bodyclose` enforces `defer resp.Body.Close()` immediately after a successful HTTP call.
- `noctx` enforces context-aware request constructors (`http.NewRequestWithContext`).
- SQL goes through `sqlc`-generated queriers. No hand-built string concatenation in business code.
- Use pointer types for nullable `Scan` targets.

## Naming and structure

- Packages: lowercase, short, no `_` or `-`. Files may use `kebab-case.go`.
- Constructors `NewX` return `*X`.
- Functional options use the `WithFoo(v T) Option` pattern that dominates `backend/pkg`.
- Interface names describe capability (`Reader`, `SqlDatabase`), not the concrete type.
- Sentinel errors: `var ErrFoo = errors.New("foo")`.

## Generated code

- `backend/gen/`, `mock_*.go`, and `sqlc`-generated files are read-only.
- Re-run `buf generate`, `sqlc generate`, or `mockery` instead of editing by hand.
